# Drive Union — Telegram Bot API server environment.
#
# Copy to /etc/drive-union-bot-api/bot-api.env, fill in every key, chmod 0600, chown root:root.
# install.sh does the copy and the permissions; the values are yours.
#
# THIS FILE'S REAL COUNTERPART NEVER GOES IN THE REPOSITORY. It carries the api_id and api_hash,
# which are credentials of the same class as the bot token. deploy/telegram-bot-api/.gitignore
# excludes *.env for exactly this reason, and that is a safety net rather than a plan.
#
# Format: systemd EnvironmentFile. KEY=value, one per line, no `export`, no shell expansion,
# no command substitution. Quotes are stripped. A stray space around the `=` is a parse error.
#
# Every key below is required and every value below is empty. install.sh refuses to enable the
# service while any of them is still empty, and names which — the alternative is a server that
# starts, listens on 0.0.0.0 because a variable expanded to nothing, and looks fine.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The credential that only self-hosting needs.
#
# From https://my.telegram.org, NOT from @BotFather. It identifies an APPLICATION registered to
# a PERSON — a phone number and a login code — not a bot. The self-hosted server is TDLib
# underneath: it speaks MTProto straight to Telegram's datacenters rather than HTTP to
# api.telegram.org, and every MTProto client has to identify itself. On the cloud API you never
# meet an api_id because Telegram's own server is that client.
#
# Whoever's account issues these is who this server is registered to, and that does not move if
# somebody else ever operates this product. See README.md § "api_id and api_hash".
#
# The bot token is a different credential entirely and does not appear in this file — it is
# pasted into the panel and stored encrypted in the database.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
TELEGRAM_API_ID=
TELEGRAM_API_HASH=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Paths. Both must be under /var/lib/drive-union-bot-api, which is the only path the unit's
# ReadWritePaths= makes writable and the only path the sweeper will delete inside. Moving
# either outside that tree means editing the unit too; install.sh checks and refuses.
#
# --dir is where the server writes every file it handles, in a subdirectory named by the bot's
# user id. --temp-dir is where it stages HTTP bodies. Both are set explicitly because a
# temporary directory left on a small root volume is the same full-disk problem discovered in a
# worse place.
#
# Recommended: /var/lib/drive-union-bot-api/work  and  /var/lib/drive-union-bot-api/tmp
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
DUBOTAPI_WORK_DIR=
DUBOTAPI_TEMP_DIR=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The listener. Nothing outside this box has any reason to reach it: the panel calls it over
# loopback, and --local lets it call the panel's webhook back over loopback. Telegram itself
# never connects inbound — this server dials out.
#
# Recommended: 127.0.0.1 and 8081. Upstream's default address is "any local IPv4 address", i.e.
# the public interface, so leaving DUBOTAPI_HTTP_IP empty is not a safe default, it is the
# unsafe one. Changing the port means changing SocketBindAllow= in the unit as well.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
DUBOTAPI_HTTP_IP=
DUBOTAPI_HTTP_PORT=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Tuning.
#
# DUBOTAPI_MAX_CONNECTIONS is upstream's --max-connections, "maximum number of open file
# descriptors". It sits under the unit's LimitNOFILE=65535. Recommended: 8192.
#
# DUBOTAPI_VERBOSITY is upstream's --verbosity, its log verbosity level. Recommended: 1.
# Raise it while diagnosing and put it back — the journal is on the volume that is this
# deployment's binding constraint.
#
# NOTHING MAY LOG A REQUEST URL AT ANY VERBOSITY. The bot token travels in the path
# (POST /bot<token>/sendMessage) and is the only authentication this server has, so a token in
# a log line is the token. Check what a raised verbosity actually prints before leaving it up.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
DUBOTAPI_MAX_CONNECTIONS=
DUBOTAPI_VERBOSITY=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Extra arguments, appended verbatim and split on whitespace. Empty contributes nothing, which
# is what keeps optional flags out of the unit file.
#
# The one worth knowing about: the server has a statistics port. Reading the pinned source's
# option list, `-s, --http-stat-port` is "HTTP statistics port" and `--http-stat-ip-address` is
# its bind address. It is off unless a port is given. If you turn it on, bind it to loopback in
# the same breath — it is as unauthenticated as the main port.
#
#   DUBOTAPI_EXTRA_ARGS=--http-stat-port 8082 --http-stat-ip-address 127.0.0.1
#
# What that port actually reports has NOT been checked by anyone here. If it carries byte
# counters it is the honest inbound measurement the Telegram spec's §13/M6 note says it has no
# source for; if it does not, that note stays unanswered.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
DUBOTAPI_EXTRA_ARGS=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The sweeper. Read by sweep-workdir.sh, not by the server.
#
# Files under the two directories above that are older than this are removed. Recommended: 30,
# matching the spec's Telegram:WorkDirMaxAgeMinutes — comfortably past the longest legitimate
# hold, which is one ceiling-sized transfer and its retries.
#
# This is a floor on how long a crashed transfer's bytes sit on the disk, not a retention
# policy. In a healthy system the panel deletes each file the instant its send completes and
# this sweeper finds nothing.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
DUBOTAPI_SWEEP_MAX_AGE_MINUTES=
